<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <div class="developer-portal">
    <header class="developer-header">
      <a href={~p"/"} class="brand"><span class="brand-icon">🌱</span>sprout<span class="brand-dot">.</span><small>for builders</small></a>
      <nav aria-label="Developer navigation">
        <a href="#quickstart">Quickstart</a><a href="#credentials">Integrations</a><a href={
          ~p"/api/openapi.json"
        }>OpenAPI ↗</a><a href={~p"/"} class="secondary-button">Back to the farm →</a>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <main class="developer-main">
      <section class="developer-hero">
        <div>
          <span class="pill">🌿 THE SPROUT DEVELOPER GARDEN</span><h1>
            Plant an integration.<br />Watch it grow.
          </h1><p>
            Connect your sensors, bring your tools, and help your farm flourish.<br />A small, thoughtful API for a very lively little world.
          </p><div class="developer-hero-actions">
            <a href="#credentials" class="primary-button">＋ Create an integration</a><a
              href={~p"/api/openapi.json"}
              class="text-button"
            >Explore the API contract ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="developer-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="orbit orbit-one"></div><div class="orbit orbit-two"></div><span class="integration-leaf">🌱</span><span class="connection-node node-water">💧</span><span class="connection-node node-sun">☀</span><span class="connection-node node-code">&lt;/&gt;</span><span class="connection-node node-flower">🌼</span><span class="connection-caption">A little connection.<br />A whole lot of possibility.</span>
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class="developer-beta">
        <span>✦ PRIVATE BETA</span><p>
          Trusted operator console · keys grant access to this farm only. This management page requires your local or private access boundary; it has no individual user login.
        </p><span class="api-version">API v1</span>
      </div>
      <section id="quickstart" class="developer-steps">
        <article>
          <span>01</span><h2>Give it a name</h2><p>
            A weather station, a research tool, a tiny side project. Every connection gets its own key.
          </p>
        </article><article>
          <span>02</span><h2>Choose its patch</h2><p>
            Grant specific fields and just the capabilities your integration needs.
          </p>
        </article><article>
          <span>03</span><h2>Send a little life</h2><p>
            Submit a sensor reading. The farm dashboard updates when it’s saved.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>
      <div :if={@notice} id="portal-notice" class="notice" role="status">🌱 {@notice}</div>
      <section :if={@new_secret} class="new-key-panel" aria-label="Your new API key">
        <span>🔑</span><div>
          <h2>Your key, fresh from the garden.</h2><p>
            Copy it now. We store only its fingerprint and cannot show it again. It expires in 90 days.
          </p><code id="new-api-key">{@new_secret}</code><button
            id="dismiss-key"
            phx-click="dismiss-key"
            class="secondary-button"
          >I saved my key ✓</button>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="credentials" class="developer-grid">
        <article class="panel developer-create">
          <p class="eyebrow">MAKE ROOM FOR SOMETHING NEW</p><h2>
            A new connection <span>🌼</span>
          </h2><p class="panel-intro">One key. A clear purpose. Only the access it needs.</p><.form
            for={@form}
            id="integration-form"
            phx-submit="create-client"
          >
            <.input
              field={@form[:name]}
              label="Integration name"
              placeholder="My little weather station"
              class="farm-input"
              required
              minlength="2"
              maxlength="100"
            /><.input
              field={@form[:field_ids]}
              type="select"
              multiple
              label="Fields it can access"
              options={@field_options}
              class="farm-input portal-multi"
              required
            /><.input
              field={@form[:scopes]}
              type="select"
              multiple
              label="Capabilities"
              options={[
                {"Read field details", "fields:read"},
                {"Read recent sensor data", "readings:read"},
                {"Send device readings", "readings:write"}
              ]}
              class="farm-input portal-multi"
              required
            /><p class="portal-help">
              Hold Ctrl / Cmd to select more than one. Keys expire after 90 days.
            </p><button class="primary-button" type="submit" disabled={!@has_fields}>Create integration →</button><p
              :if={!@has_fields}
              class="portal-help"
            >
              Add a field on your farm before issuing a key.
            </p>
          </.form>
        </article>
        <article class="panel developer-clients">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">YOUR CONNECTED LITTLE WORLD</p><h2>Growing connections</h2>
            </div><span class="soft-tag">{@client_count} integrations</span>
          </div><div id="integration-clients" phx-update="stream">
            <div :if={@client_count == 0} id="clients-empty" class="portal-empty">
              <span>🌿</span><h3>A lovely place to start.</h3><p>
                Your first connection is waiting to put down roots.
              </p>
            </div><article
              :for={{dom_id, client} <- @streams.clients}
              id={dom_id}
              class="integration-client"
            >
              <div class="client-title">
                <strong>{client.name}</strong><span class={"client-status status-#{String.downcase(status(client))}"}>{status(
                  client
                )}</span>
              </div><code>{client.token_prefix}…</code><p>
                {Enum.map_join(client.fields, " · ", & &1.name)}
              </p><div class="scope-tags"><span :for={scope <- client.scopes}>{scope}</span></div><div class="client-footer">
                <small>Expires {Calendar.strftime(client.expires_at, "%b %d, %Y")}</small><button
                  :if={status(client) == "Active"}
                  id={"revoke-client-#{client.id}"}
                  class="revoke-button"
                  phx-click="revoke-client"
                  phx-value-id={client.id}
                >Revoke key</button>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>
      <section class="developer-examples">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <h2>A first little hello <span>👋</span></h2><p>
              Set SPROUT_API_KEY in your shell. Keep it out of source control.
            </p>
          </div><span class="soft-tag">JSON over HTTP</span>
        </div><div class="example-grid">
          <article>
            <div class="code-title">
              <span class="method method-get">GET</span><strong>Your fields</strong><small>fields:read</small>
            </div><pre><code>{list_example(@api_base)}</code></pre><p>
              The response contains only the fields granted to your key.
            </p>
          </article><article>
            <div class="code-title">
              <span class="method method-post">POST</span><strong>A sensor reading</strong><small>readings:write</small>
            </div><pre><code>{write_example(@api_base)}</code></pre><p>
              Set FIELD_ID to a granted field. Use a unique key for each sample; reuse it only when retrying the same payload.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="developer-reference panel">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">SMALL CONTRACT. CLEAR EXPECTATIONS.</span><h2>
            Everything you need to connect.
          </h2><p>
            Download the OpenAPI contract for schemas, scopes, units, and error responses.
          </p>
        </div><a href={~p"/api/openapi.json"} class="secondary-button">Open API specification ↗</a>
      </section>
      <div class="api-facts">
        <p>
          💧 Moisture & humidity in percent · 🌡 Temperature in °C · 🚿 Water in liters per interval
        </p><p>
          201 new sample · 200 replay · 401 invalid key · 403 missing scope · 404 unavailable field · 409 retry conflict · 422 invalid data
        </p>
      </div>
      <footer>
        Built for curious minds & thriving fields.<span>🌱 Sprout · A little more connected.</span>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
